    <GaugingStation location="Saltersford Total" name="Witham" number="30005">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Compound structure gauging a rural catchment u/s of Grantham, mixed geology and significant artificial influences.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">Discharge computed from a single stage recorder to 1973, when it was discovered that a trout screen diverted flow over high flow weir. Second recorder installed, which was removed in Feb 1985 when trout screen was removed. One rating applied across period of record.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Compound weir with round-crested low flow weir, 1.83m wide, and broad-crested high flow portion, 8.25m wide. The Measuring Authority recorded these structures separately until 1985.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow record">Data prior to 1973 should not be used; data from 1973 to 1985 calculated from addition of high &amp; low flow weir. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2020 (WINFAP Files v9).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Flow regime">Runoff influenced by groundwater abstraction/recharge. Major abstractions for PWS immediately u/s, with significant effect on low flows.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">Flat catchment, underlain by limestone and clay with about quarter of the area covered with Boulder Clay on east margin and in south. Predominantly rural.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff">RPGI</Comment>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged to within 27% of QMED. Reasonable fit to gaugings." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Few high flow gaugings. Rating can not be validated beyond QMED when weir is likely to drown." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
